Title:  To choose one's attitude

Seq:    12.6.60.1.2

Level:  6 - Subdetail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Frankl, Victor|Victor Frankl]], 1946, from the book *[[Man's Search for Meaning]]*

Timestamp: 20251216213208

Date Added: 2025-12-16 14:32:08 -0700

Date Modified: 2026-10-15 12:27:06 -0600

Referenced In: We each manage four interrelated realms

Body:

Everything can be taken from a man but one thing: the last of the human freedoms -- to choose one's attitude in any given set of circumstances, to choose one's own way. 

